# Normalize line endings. OneDrive on Windows keeps flipping LF↔CRLF in the working tree, which
# produced whole-file "churn" diffs that twice masked (and once discarded) real one-line changes.
# With this, Git stores LF in the repo and checks out LF, so `git diff` shows only real changes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary/rendered assets Git must never try to normalize.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
